link.feishu.cn/client/todo/detail?guid=381a196d-a437-4c56-9afc-daba109971b5&suite_entity_num=t133892"},{"completed_at":"1765445063905","created_at":"1764469270849","creator":{"id":"ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409","type":"user"},"dependencies":[],"description":"基于效果评估结果优化唤醒策略，建立客户分层维护机制及预防沉睡预警体系","due":{"is_all_day":false,"timestamp":"1764485999000"},"extra":"","guid":"b824fe6d-8ecf-49af-b210-2b52dd1b0c91","is_milestone":false,"members":[{"id":"ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409","role":"assignee","type":"user"}],"mode":2,"origin":{"href":{"title":"飞书Aily","url":"https://aily.feishu.cn/ai/ailyplay"},"platform_i18n_name":{"de_de":"","en_us":"Feishu Aily","es_es":"","fr_fr":"","it_it":"","ja_jp":"","ko_kr":"","ru_ru":"","th_th":"","zh_cn":"飞书Aily","zh_hk":"","zh_tw":""}},"parent_task_guid":"","repeat_rule":"","source":7,"status":"done","subtask_count":0,"summary":"方案优化：长效客户激活机制制定","task_id":"t133456","tasklists":[],"updated_at":"1765445064104","url":"https://applink.feishu.cn/client/todo/detail?guid=b824fe6d-8ecf-49af-b210-2b52dd1b0c91&suite_entity_num=t133456"}],"has_more":true,"page_token":"CghMaXN0VGFzaxAUGI6Dyo3ZMw--"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1776265888631}}
{"type":"message","id":"3e7b4ad7","parentId":"2359d534","timestamp":"2026-04-15T15:11:55.235Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the task data. The current time is 2026-04-15T15:11:00Z (UTC), which is 2026-04-15T23:11:00+08:00 (Beijing time).\n\nThe bitable (shared pool progress table) returned a \"WrongTableId\" error. I need to find the correct table ID.\n\nLet me first analyze which tasks might be \"dead\" (no update in 60+ minutes). The task监督与检查 task was updated at 1774826680144ms which converts to around 2026-04-01 - that's well over 60 minutes ago. But it's already completed so it doesn't matter.\n \nNow I'm converting the remaining task timestamps. The 每周循环提醒 task was updated around 2026-04-08, while 任务监督与检查 is much more recent at 2026-04-09, and the third task dates back to 2026-04-01 - so that last one is definitely stale. Now I'm converting these millisecond timestamps to readable dates—the first one corresponds to January 2026, the second is from February 2026, and the third also appears to be from January based on the pattern I'm seeing with the Unix epoch conversions. Looking at the task timestamps, all the Aily tasks appear to be from around January 2026 based on the milliseconds conversion, so they're not actually stale. But the third task with ID 1769829129694 definitely seems old given the context of the conversation being from February. Let me convert the current timestamp to verify what day it actually is. 2026-04-15 23:11:00 CST.\n\nNow I'm comparing the task timestamps to see if any are stale. Looking at the timestamps, most of the recent ones are from April 2026, but a few stand out as significantly older—particularly t135657 at 1769829129694 which converts to around January 1, 2026, and t135508 which is even earlier, both clearly stale and past the 60-minute threshold.\n\nFor t135256, the timestamp 1768890033543 appears to be from February 2026, so that's also stale. The tasks t134635 and t134634 have nearly identical timestamps around 1767497992692 and 1767497479436, both from early January 2026, and t134449 at 1766728812919 is similarly old.\n\nThe Aily tasks cluster around 1767164696588 to 1767164709265, all from January 2026, so they're all stale. The third task at 1765445063905 is from late December 2025, also stale. The fourth task at 1765235930441 is from December 2025.\n\nLooking at the newer tasks, t133456 at 1764469270849 is from December 2025, which is also stale.\n\nSo I'm seeing a pattern here—most of these tasks are from late 2025 and early 2026, with just a couple from April 2026 being current.\n\nSince the cron job mentioned a task board, I should probably check if there's a bitable board in the shared pool that's more actively maintained than these stale tasks. The search results mentioned a bitable called \"德胧AI共享池-项目进度管理表\" which seems like it might be the active task board I should be looking at instead.\n\nI need to query the bitable to find the right table and get a proper view of current tasks, then decide whether these old tasks with their outdated dates should be marked as completed or left as-is since the cron job was specifically about checking the task board itself.\n\nLooking at the timestamps, I see that t135256 was created in January 2026 and hasn't been touched since then—that's definitely stale. The other tasks like the one about hotel operations data are marked as recurring weekly tasks with future due dates, so those aren't actually overdue. The key distinction is between tasks that are truly abandoned versus ones that are just on hold or waiting for future action. The old tasks from 2025 aren't showing up as completed, so marking them as dead without user confirmation seems risky. I'm wondering if the cron job itself is meant to identify and mark stale tasks automatically. I should try accessing the bitable directly to get the actual task board data instead of relying on the incomplete task list. After that, I'll update the heartbeat state and figure out what needs to go into the progress report for the shared pool."},{"type":"text","text":"Let me get the bitable tables list to find the correct table ID for the shared pool progress table.\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ctjkxdgae9rh_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table","arguments":{"action":"list","app_token":"TeIZbungWasADfsKcnjcogmMnCd"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ctjkxdgae9rh_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /home/gem/workspace/agent/workspace/memory/daily/2026-04-15.md 2>/dev/null | head -50 || echo \"File not found\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776265888636,"responseId":"062edda04949b377bef4ce65a49d6b5f"}}
